WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.942
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Cambodia Grade twelve English.

2
00:00:06.242 --> 00:00:09.814
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:10.114 --> 00:00:17.213
Unit twelve: Word Formation: Prefixes and Suffixes. Today you will build new words from a root word.

4
00:00:17.513 --> 00:00:20.259
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:24.607
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.450 --> 00:00:26.544
Prefix.

7
00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:29.956
Prefix means letters added at the start.

8
00:00:30.550 --> 00:00:31.934
Un- is a prefix.

9
00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:35.063
Your turn. Say: Prefix.

10
00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:38.878
Prefix.

11
00:00:39.617 --> 00:00:40.734
Suffix.

12
00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:44.051
Suffix means letters added at the end.

13
00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:46.081
-ful is a suffix.

14
00:00:46.683 --> 00:00:49.278
Your turn. Say: Suffix.

15
00:00:52.133 --> 00:00:53.204
Suffix.

16
00:00:53.950 --> 00:00:54.626
Root.

17
00:00:55.617 --> 00:00:57.802
Root means the basic part of a word.

18
00:00:58.417 --> 00:00:59.638
The root is happy.

19
00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:02.566
Your turn. Say: Root.

20
00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:06.285
Root.

21
00:01:07.050 --> 00:01:08.156
Unhappy.

22
00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:10.883
Unhappy means not happy.

23
00:01:11.483 --> 00:01:12.879
He was unhappy.

24
00:01:13.483 --> 00:01:15.985
Your turn. Say: Unhappy.

25
00:01:18.833 --> 00:01:19.869
Unhappy.

26
00:01:20.617 --> 00:01:21.432
Careful.

27
00:01:22.417 --> 00:01:24.091
Careful means taking care.

28
00:01:24.683 --> 00:01:25.708
Be careful.

29
00:01:26.317 --> 00:01:28.934
Your turn. Say: Careful.

30
00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:32.627
Careful.

31
00:01:33.383 --> 00:01:34.303
Decision.

32
00:01:35.317 --> 00:01:37.409
Decision means a choice made.

33
00:01:38.017 --> 00:01:39.505
It was a good decision.

34
00:01:40.117 --> 00:01:42.769
Your turn. Say: Decision.

35
00:01:45.633 --> 00:01:46.507
Decision.

36
00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:48.390
Impossible.

37
00:01:49.383 --> 00:01:51.534
Impossible means not possible.

38
00:01:52.150 --> 00:01:53.488
It is impossible.

39
00:01:54.083 --> 00:01:56.562
Your turn. Say: Impossible.

40
00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:00.633
Impossible.

41
00:02:01.383 --> 00:02:02.350
Development.

42
00:02:03.350 --> 00:02:04.978
Development means growth.

43
00:02:05.583 --> 00:02:07.072
Economic development.

44
00:02:07.683 --> 00:02:10.057
Your turn. Say: Development.

45
00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:13.971
Development.

46
00:02:14.767 --> 00:02:18.406
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:19.250 --> 00:02:21.517
Visal, how do I form new words?

48
00:02:22.617 --> 00:02:38.182
Add a prefix or a suffix to a root word. Happy becomes unhappy with un-, and care becomes careful with -ful. A prefix changes the meaning; a suffix often changes the word class.

49
00:02:39.283 --> 00:02:41.016
Which suffixes make nouns?

50
00:02:42.117 --> 00:02:53.903
Common noun suffixes are -tion, -ment, -ness and -ity: decide becomes decision, develop becomes development, kind becomes kindness.

51
00:02:55.017 --> 00:02:56.714
How do I use this in an exam?

52
00:02:57.817 --> 00:03:09.339
Read the sentence and decide what word class is missing: a noun, an adjective, an adverb or a verb. Then add the right suffix and check spelling.

53
00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:12.360
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:13.217 --> 00:03:16.633
Grammar focus: root plus prefix and suffix.

55
00:03:16.933 --> 00:03:18.154
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:18.850 --> 00:03:20.757
happy → unhappy.

57
00:03:21.650 --> 00:03:23.383
care → careful.

58
00:03:24.333 --> 00:03:31.641
A prefix changes the meaning and a suffix often changes the word class. Decide which class is needed before you choose.

59
00:03:32.383 --> 00:03:35.570
Be careful! Don't say: He is a care student.

60
00:03:37.533 --> 00:03:40.067
Say: He is a careful student.

61
00:03:40.367 --> 00:03:41.867
Add the right suffix.

62
00:03:42.667 --> 00:03:45.261
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:46.067 --> 00:03:47.497
A Careful Student.

64
00:03:47.797 --> 00:03:49.739
Visal is a careful student.

65
00:03:50.733 --> 00:03:53.348
He made a wise decision to study every day.

66
00:03:54.333 --> 00:03:56.623
It was impossible to finish without help.

67
00:03:57.633 --> 00:03:59.830
Her kindness made him feel welcome.

68
00:04:00.833 --> 00:04:02.972
The development of his English was clear.

69
00:04:04.067 --> 00:04:08.080
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:08.917 --> 00:04:10.115
Un- is a blank.

71
00:04:10.415 --> 00:04:14.103
A, prefix. B, suffix. C, root.

72
00:04:17.667 --> 00:04:19.747
The answer is A: prefix.

73
00:04:20.883 --> 00:04:22.964
Care + ful = blank.

74
00:04:23.264 --> 00:04:26.558
A, caring. B, careful. C, carely.

75
00:04:30.100 --> 00:04:31.949
The answer is B: careful.

76
00:04:33.083 --> 00:04:35.083
Decide → blank (noun).

77
00:04:35.383 --> 00:04:39.152
A, decisive. B, decided. C, decision.

78
00:04:42.700 --> 00:04:44.525
The answer is C: decision.

79
00:04:45.683 --> 00:04:46.893
Im- means blank.

80
00:04:47.193 --> 00:04:50.533
A, not. B, very. C, again.

81
00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:56.181
The answer is A: not.

82
00:04:57.317 --> 00:04:59.397
Develop → blank (noun).

83
00:04:59.697 --> 00:05:03.200
A, developing. B, development. C, developed.

84
00:05:06.733 --> 00:05:09.209
The answer is B: development.

85
00:05:10.400 --> 00:05:13.726
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:14.583 --> 00:05:17.012
Make nouns from: kind, decide, move.

87
00:05:25.817 --> 00:05:27.294
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:27.594 --> 00:05:37.888
Kind becomes kindness, decide becomes decision and move becomes movement. I change the suffix to make a noun. I also check the spelling.

89
00:05:38.188 --> 00:05:39.805
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:40.717 --> 00:05:45.517
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and root plus prefix and suffix.

91
00:05:45.817 --> 00:05:50.919
Today's value is precision of language. Choose your words carefully so others understand you.

92
00:05:51.219 --> 00:05:53.929
See you in Unit thirteen. Goodbye!

93
00:05:54.229 --> 00:05:57.160
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

